ps on opposite sides — either on the left and right walls (train 1, train 2 first frame, test frame at top-left) or on the top and bottom walls (train 3, train 2 second frame, the two remaining test frames). The bumps are centred on their walls. Inside each frame sits a red (2) motif that occupies only one half of the interior.\n\nIn every output the red motif has been reflected across the middle of the interior, along the axis the bumps point along, and both the original and its mirror image are drawn. Train 1: the `2 2 / 2 . / 2 2` bracket at x=4..5 gains its left-right mirror at x=6..7 (bumps on left/right). Train 3: the three-row motif at y=5..7 gains its up-down mirror at y=8..10 (bumps on top/bottom). The bumps act as a legend telling us the reflection direction; nothing else in the grid changes, and the frame itself stays put.\n\n## How the program finds the geometry\n\n1. Flood-fill the non-8 cells that touch the grid border: that is the outside. Everything non-8 inside a frame's bounding box that is not outside is the frame's interior (including the tiny cells behind the bumps).\n2. For the interior, count how many rows reach the maximal row width and how many columns reach the maximal column height. If fewer rows than columns are maximal, the bumps are on the left/right and we mirror horizontally about `ix0+ix1-x`; otherwise we mirror vertically about `iy0+iy1-y`, where `(iy0,ix0,iy1,ix1)` is the interior bounding box. The bumps being centred guarantees the interior box is symmetric about the right axis.\n3. Copy every non-background interior cell to its mirror partner (keeping the originals).\n\nFor the test input: the top-left frame has side bumps at rows 5–7, so its `2 / 2 2 / 2` motif at x=5..6 is mirrored to the right half; the top-right frame has top/bottom bumps (column 21) so its arch motif at y=7..9 is mirrored downward to y=10..12 — wait, its interior spans y=3..10 so it maps y=7..9 to y=6..4; and the bottom frame (bump at column 11, interior y=16..23) maps its y=17..19 motif to y=22..20. Each frame is handled independently and emitted as its own stage.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    bg = background(g)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    emit(g, \"Start from the input: blue frames with bumps, each holding a red motif in one half.\")\n    outside = set()\n    for comp in components(g != 8):\n        if any(y in (0, H - 1) or x in (0, W - 1) for y, x in comp):\n            outside |= set(comp)\n    for o in objects(g, bg):\n        if o[\"colour\"] != 8:\n            continue\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        inner = [(y, x) for y in range(y0, y1 + 1) for x in range(x0, x1 + 1)\n                 if g[y, x] != 8 and (y, x) not in outside]\n        if not inner:\n            continue\n        iy0, ix0, iy1, ix1 = bbox(inner)\n        rw = {}\n        ch = {}\n        for y, x in inner:\n            rw[y] = rw.get(y, 0) + 1\n            ch[x] = ch.get(x, 0) + 1\n        n_rows_max = sum(1 for v in rw.values() if v == max(rw.values()))\n        n_cols_max = sum(1 for v in ch.values() if v == max(ch.values()))\n        horiz = n_rows_max < n_cols_max\n        src = [(y, x) for y, x in inner if g[y, x] != bg]\n        for y, x in src:\n            if horiz:\n                g[y, ix0 + ix1 - x] = g[y, x]\n            else:\n                g[iy0 + iy1 - y, x] = g[y, x]\n        emit(g, (\"Frame at rows %d-%d, cols %d-%d has bumps on the %s walls: mirror its red motif \"\n                 \"across the interior centre %s and keep both copies.\")\n             % (y0, y1, x0, x1, \"left/right\" if horiz else \"top/bottom\",\n                \"horizontally\" if horiz else \"vertically\"))\n    emit(g, \"All frames completed: every motif is now symmetric along its bump axis.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":" the maximal extent: with side bumps only the few bump rows are widest while almost every column is tallest; with top/bottom bumps almost every row is widest while only the bump column(s) are tallest."}],"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The bumps act as a legend telling us the reflection direction; nothing else in the grid changes, and the frame itself stays put."}],"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every output the red motif has been reflected across the middle of the interior, along the axis the bumps point along, and both the original and its mirror image are drawn."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Train 1: the `2 2 / 2 . / 2 2` bracket at x=4..5 gains its left-right mirror at x=6..7 (bumps on left/right)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Train 3: the three-row motif at y=5..7 gains its up-down mirror at y=8..10 (bumps on top/bottom)."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Inside each frame sits a red (2) motif that occupies only one half of the interior."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every output the red motif has been reflected across the middle of the interior, along the axis the bumps point along, and both the original and its mirror image are drawn."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Train 3: the three-row motif at y=5..7 gains its up-down mirror at y=8..10 (bumps on top/bottom)."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Inside each frame sits a red (2) motif that occupies only one half of the interior."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In every output the red motif has been reflected across the middle of the interior, along the axis the bumps point along, and both the original and its mirror image are drawn."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Flood-fill the non-8 cells that touch the grid border: that is the outside."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"For the interior, count how many rows reach the maximal row width and how many columns reach the maximal column height."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Everything non-8 inside a frame's bounding box that is not outside is the frame's interior (including the tiny cells behind the bumps)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"ix1-x`; otherwise we mirror vertically about `iy0+iy1-y`, where `(iy0,ix0,iy1,ix1)` is the interior bounding box."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Train 3: the three-row motif at y=5..7 gains its up-down mirror at y=8..10 (bumps on top/bottom)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"308c7f6c44d55f63d8a3589c85edec33f5e9a9f3a81c0452a71461ad3aa6eab8","task_sha256":"16f7e62580959f8b629b2f8045fc0c9344db10f51ecac09e1330350b68016ce3","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
